    description: "PR-1 of the inherited_calls campaign (parent META INV-nilud). Pure additive refactor — no behavior change, no bakeoff.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. `analyze/base.py:445`: extend `make_unresolved_edge(...)` with three optional kwargs: `enclosing_class: str | None`, `receiver_type_hint: str | None`, `inherited_field_receiver: str | None`. They land in `Edge.meta`. Existing call sites unchanged at default.\n2. `linkers/inheritance.py:34-127`: promote `_resolve_target_symbol` → public `resolve_target_symbol`. (Same-language gating + same-file preference + sorted-ID fallback.)\n3. `linkers/method_call_recovery.py`: promote `_short_name` → `short_name`, `_parse_unresolved_name` → `parse_unresolved_name`.\n4. `linkers/_transitive_bases.py:113-126`: generalize `build_inheritance_index(edges)` → `build_inheritance_index(edges, edge_types: tuple[str, ...] = (\"extends\", \"implements\"))`. Existing callers pass through default; PR-2 will pass `(\"extends\", \"implements\", \"includes\")` for Ruby.\n5. `linkers/type_hierarchy.py:291-330`: extract `_TypeHierarchyIndex` build into a module-public `build_method_index(...)` helper so PR-2's `inherited_calls.py` reuses it without a circular ordering dependency.\n\n**Tests:** existing tests must pass unchanged (no behavior change). New helper signatures get direct-call unit tests in their current packages. 100% coverage required.\n\n**No bakeoff:** pure refactor, behavior-preserving. No `awaits_bakeoff_validation` tag.\n\nCanonical plan: `~/puluf-plan.md`."  # 140e
    fields: {}  # 140e
